    27	
    28	```text
    29	9.9 is larger than 9.11.
    30	```
    31	
    32	stderr, the reasoning:
    33	
    34	```text
    35	The user is asking me to compare two numbers: 9.11 and 9.9, and answer in one sentence.
    36	...
    37	When comparing decimals, 9.90 > 9.11 (since 0.90 > 0.11)
    38	```
    39	
    40	The split matters. stdout carries the answer, so a pipe stays clean, and the reasoning goes
    41	to stderr. No `<thinking>` tag reached either stream.
    42	
    43	## 2. A two-call tool loop, with thinking on
    44	
    45	Sprint 1 found that Bedrock worked for one tool call and answered 400 for two. Anthropic also
    46	documents that a thinking block must be replayed inside a tool loop, and rho does not replay
    47	one yet. So this run tested the risk rather than assuming it.
    48	
    49	```sh
    50	printf 'zx9-quibble\n' > a.txt; printf 'kt4-marlow\n' > b.txt
    51	rho run "Use your tools. Read a.txt, then read b.txt, then print the two exact strings you \
    52	found, separated by a comma." --provider bedrock --model "$M" \
    53	  --reasoning-effort high --reasoning full
